## 1. Scope

The previous local-first theorem proved that compatible linear states form a
Cech equalizer rather than a tensor product over patches. This theorem lifts
that statement one level upstream, to nonlinear repair.

It does not postulate a physical collapse law. It proves the exact descent
conditions under which local nonlinear repair fields, their fixed points and
their asymptotic basin maps define one global object. It also identifies the
extra premise needed before such an asymptotic map may be called a unique
actualization rule.

## 2. Nonlinear repair descent theorem

Let `M_i` be local Riemannian configuration charts, `E_i` local Hermitian
defect spaces, and let

```text
U_ij:M_i -> M_j,
V_ij:E_i -> E_j
```

be respectively Riemannian isometries and unitary defect transitions. Suppose
the selected nonlinear defect maps obey

```text
Phi_j o U_ij = V_ij o Phi_i.
```

Define

```text
C_i(x)=1/2 ||Phi_i(x)||^2,
X_i(x)=-grad C_i(x).
```

Unitarity gives `C_j o U_ij=C_i`. Differentiating this equality and using that
`U_ij` is an isometry gives

```text
T U_ij X_i = X_j o U_ij.
```

Uniqueness of the local initial-value problem then gives the flow identity

```text
U_ij o R_i(t) = R_j(t) o U_ij.
```

Consequently the product repair flow preserves the nonlinear Cech equalizer

```text
Gamma(M)={x_i : x_j=U_ij x_i on every overlap}.
```

Zeros of the defect, critical points and fixed points therefore descend.

## 3. Basin-limit and conditional actualization functor

Let `p_i` be compatible fixed points and suppose the forward limit exists on
their attraction basins:

```text
A_i(x)=lim_(t->infinity) R_i(t)x.
```

Continuity of `U_ij` and flow intertwining imply

```text
A_j o U_ij = U_ij o A_i.
```

Thus the local limit maps descend to

```text
A:Gamma(Basin) -> Gamma(Fix).
```

This is the conditional actualization functor: it turns an already supplied
compatible initial section into its compatible asymptotic fixed section.

The basin labels themselves form a local system. A single-valued global basin
label is a label fixed by every cycle holonomy. Hence

```text
global basin labels = intersection_gamma Fix(Hol_gamma on local labels).
```

They are not the Cartesian product of the local label sets. If exactly one
attracting label is holonomy-fixed and every allowed global initial state lies
in its basin, then the descended asymptotic outcome is unique. Those are
premises of the theorem, not facts supplied automatically by Hilbert space,
unitarity or projection.

## 4. Linearization is recovered, not replaced

At a compatible zero-defect fixed point `p_i`, set

```text
L_i=D Phi_i(p_i).
```

The already proved squared-defect identity gives

```text
H_i=Hess C_i(p_i)=L_i^* L_i.
```

Differentiating overlap equivariance gives conjugate local Hessians:

```text
H_j T U_ij = T U_ij H_i.
```

Therefore the tangent repair semigroups and their coherent projectors preserve
the linear Cech equalizer. The earlier Cech-Hilbert theorem is exactly the
linearization of the nonlinear descent statement.

